<figure class="pw-figure" data-wal-progress aria-labelledby="pw-progress-title">
  <figcaption id="pw-progress-title"><span>Figure 1</span><strong>One history, three progress points</strong></figcaption>
  <label class="pw-option">Commit setting <select aria-label="Commit setting for figure 1"><option value="on">synchronous_commit = on</option><option value="off">synchronous_commit = off</option></select></label>
  <div class="pw-axis"><span>Earlier WAL</span><span>U · update</span><span>C · commit</span></div>
  <div class="pw-progress-rows">
    {['Inserted · WAL buffers','Written · WAL file','Flushed · durable storage'].map((label,i)=><div class="pw-track"><strong>{label}</strong><div class="pw-cells" data-row={i} data-live><span>Earlier</span><span>U</span><span>C</span></div></div>)}
  </div>
  <div class="pw-result"><span>Application heard</span><strong data-ack data-live>Waiting</strong><span>Data page in its file</span><strong>May still hold 20.00</strong></div>
  <p class="pw-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite"></p>
  <div class="pw-controls" role="group" aria-label="Playback for figure 1"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step></span><div data-hold><span></span></div></div>
  <p class="pw-caption">A selected schedule for the logged P7 price update, with reliable surviving storage and no synchronous standby. U and C stand for records, not actual WAL encodings or measured LSNs. Each ticked cell means that progress has reached the end of that record. Writes and flushes may happen earlier than drawn.</p>
  <details><summary>Figure as text</summary><ol><li>The update inserts U into WAL buffers.</li><li>Commit inserts C. With off, the application can hear success already.</li><li>The records are written to the WAL file, which can leave bytes in an operating-system cache.</li><li>A flush makes the required records durable. With on, success can now be acknowledged.</li></ol><p>At every step a data page can lag behind the durable WAL. The commit wait is for WAL, not for every changed data page.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
  import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-wal-progress]').forEach(root => {
    const option = root.querySelector('select')!;
    const explanations = [
      'Earlier WAL is already durable. P7 starts at 20.00. The update and its commit record have not been inserted.',
      'UPDATE changes P7 to 22.00 in a shared buffer and inserts U into WAL buffers. Inserting is not writing or flushing.',
      'COMMIT inserts C. The records are still only in memory in this schedule.',
      'PostgreSQL writes U and C to the WAL file. The operating system may still hold them in volatile memory.',
      'The required WAL through C is flushed. The storage contract now protects the commit; the data page can be written later.'
    ];
    const player = stepper(root, { steps:()=>5, draw:(step:number)=>{
      const off = option.value === 'off';
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-row]').forEach((row,i)=>{
        const reached = i===0 ? (step>=2?2:step>=1?1:0) : i===1 ? (step>=3?2:0) : (step>=4?2:0);
        row.querySelectorAll('span').forEach((cell,j)=>{
          cell.classList.toggle('pw-reached',j<=reached);
          cell.textContent=(j<=reached?'✓ ':'')+['Earlier','U','C'][j];
        });
      });
      root.querySelector('[data-ack]')!.textContent=(off?step>=2:step>=4)?'COMMIT succeeded':'Waiting';
      root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=explanations[step]+(step===2?(off?' With off, the reply can leave now. A crash can still lose the price change.':' With on, the application keeps waiting for the required local flush.'):'');
    }});
    option.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render());
  });
</script>
